    "correction_rule": "An explicit later correction updates only its stated owner and topic. Do not universally prefer the last clause; simultaneous admissibility and reluctance are distinct predicates.",
    "predicate_notes": {
      "mortgage_permission": "Current permission to consider mortgage, not desire or a selected financing scheme.",
      "mortgage_use": "Client-stated future financing plan. An unresolved choice is UNKNOWN, explicit inclusion is YES and explicit exclusion is NO. No objective future outcome is predicted.",
      "dp_current_available_some": "Existence of at least some currently available DP funds. Partial funding is YES. A particular unavailable amount does not deny all other funds. A future inflow does not prove current absence.",
      "dp_future_funds_available": "Explicit expected later availability/inflow of DP funds, including after a named event. This is the client expectation, not independent financial verification. Current availability or amount alone leaves the future UNKNOWN.",
      "ownership": "Relative facts stay attributed to the named relative. An unspecified client fact is UNKNOWN, not NO. Age-restricted absence does not imply absence of all children.",
      "budget": "Preserve only the amount/range and owner stated. Do not add currency absent from the text. Foreign-budget negation is not a comparison against a separate client budget.",
      "criteria": "Distinguish desire, importance and obligation. Optional is not unwanted; not essential is not unimportant.",
      "goals": "Rental, personal use and permanent residence are separate atomic questions. Their answers may coexist; no exclusive product taxonomy is inferred."
    }
